--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Transparency Issues (Matt)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

There's no good way to do transparency other than adding all Geometry
together and sorting it.  Right now I sort the Geometry independently.
That means you can't have multiple transparent surfaces in the file
and expect them to work together.  The correct solution is for any
transparent render to register itself on a Geometry chain, then to
sort and draw the chain at the end of the rendering cycle.

Another possibility is Depth Peeling Rendering, which blends together
many depth-masked renders.  I didn't have time to debug this to a
working state but the pieces are in DepthPeelingRenderer.cpp

